{
  "payloads": [
    {
      "text": "**The Seven Deaths of Evelyn Hardcastle** by **Stuart Turton** was published in **2018** by **Sourcebooks Landmark**. The ISBN for the book is **978-1-4926-6854-6**. \n\n### Overview\nThe novel features a unique narrative structure where the protagonist relives the same day multiple times, each time from the perspective of a different guest at the Blackheath estate. He attempts to solve the murder of Evelyn Hardcastle before the day resets again. This blending of a traditional Agatha Christie-style country house mystery with a time-loop framework adds depth to themes concerning perspective, identity, and moral responsibility.\n\n### Awards and Nominations\nWhile specific awards are not detailed in the search results, the novel has been recognized and praised within literary circles, suggesting it garnered significant critical attention upon publication. It has become an essential text within its genre.\n\n### Positioning in the Mystery Genre\nTurton’s work has been noted for its recursive narrative structure and compelling approach to perspective and identity within the mystery genre. Reviewers have highlighted its innovative blend of elements that resonate with classic mystery tropes while presenting a modern twist. This positioning has allowed it to stand out in discussions about contemporary mysteries.\n\nFor further detailed insights, you can visit these sources:\n- [Wikipedia Entry on The Seven Deaths of Evelyn Hardcastle](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Seven_Deaths_of_Evelyn_Hardcastle)\n- [Critical Overview of The Seven Deaths of Evelyn Hardcastle](https://openbooks.net/reviews/seven-deaths-of-evelyn-hardcastle)\n\nThis information should help you shape your seminar module effectively!",
      "mediaUrl": null
    }
